HOW TO START THE BLOCK NATIONS PLAY-BY-POST SERVER (LOCAL)

# Local PBp Server Setup (Development Only)

This guide explains how to run the Play-by-Post server locally for testing.
For production/VPS instructions, see Notion docs.

1) REQUIREMENTS
- Node.js installed (https://nodejs.org, LTS is fine)
- Port 8080 must be free

2) OPEN TERMINAL (macOS)
Cmd + Space → type "Terminal" → Enter

3) GO TO THE PROJECT FOLDER
cd /Users/Jo/Documents/GitHub/BlockNations

4) START THE SERVER
node server.js

You should see something like:
[pbp] server listening on 0.0.0.0:8080

Leave this terminal open while playing.

5) VERIFY SERVER IS RUNNING
In a NEW terminal window, run:
curl http://127.0.0.1:8080/healthz

Expected output:
{"ok":true}

6) FIND LOCAL IP (FOR IPHONE / OTHER DEVICES)
ipconfig getifaddr en0

Example output:
192.168.0.27

Use this address in the game:
http://192.168.0.27:8080

7) HOSTING A GAME (IN BLOCK NATIONS)
- Start the game
- Choose "Multiplayer by Post"
- Click "Create Game"
- Game code is copied to clipboard
- Send the game code to the other player

8) JOINING A GAME
- Start the game on another device/editor
- Choose "Multiplayer by Post"
- Click "Join Game"
- Paste the game code
- Game shows "Waiting for opponent"

9) IMPORTANT NOTES
- The server must stay running (do NOT close the terminal)
- USB cable is NOT required after installing the iOS app
- Devices must be on the SAME Wi-Fi network
- This setup is LAN-only (no internet play yet)

10) STOP THE SERVER
In the terminal running the server, press:
Ctrl + C

TROUBLESHOOTING
- If curl /healthz fails → server is not running
- If iPhone cannot connect → check Wi-Fi, IP address, firewall